            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for to baptise, then the German for the christening."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: aufwachsen",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aufwachsen — \"to grow up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ich bin auf dem Land aufgewachsen. I grew up in the country."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Separable, strong, with sein: wuchs auf, ist aufgewachsen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aufwachsen joins auf \"up\" and wachsen \"to grow\", from Proto-Germanic wahsijaną (EtymDB), a cousin of English wax."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
